==English==
{{wikipedia}} [[Image:Ajedrez captura al paso del peon.png|frame|En passant in chess]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|en passant}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɒn paˈsɒ̃/|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In [[passing]]; [[incidentally]]; [[by the way]].
# {{label|en|chess}} Describing a special kind of pawn [[capture]], whereby a [[pawn]] [[capture]]s an opposing pawn immediately after it has moved forward two [[squares]] from its initial position as if it had moved only one square; the opposing pawn is captured "in [[passing]] through" the usual square from where it would ordinarily be liable to be captured.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|chess}} A [[move]] in which a [[pawn]] [[capture]]s an opposing pawn on the same [[rank]] immediately after the latter moved two [[squares]] from its initial position as if it had moved only one square.
#* {{quote-book|year=2007|author=Mark Borders|title=The Self-Improvement of Chess|page=12|publisher=Lulu|url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=5t9KYWJJyw8C&pg=PA12&dq=%22en+passant+is%22&hl=cs&sa=X&ved=0CE4Q6AEwB2oVChMI7vn5k8SFyQIVQvByCh2l5wPW#v=onepage&q=%22en%20passant%20is%22&f=false|isbn=978-1-4303-2764-6|passage='''En passant''' is the rarest of moves.}}

